Zoe (SDK): Draft TS snippet for the 429 retry (TS SDK >=3.2):
```ts
// Retry-After > x-rw-retry, exponential backoff
async function sendWithRetry(req){
  for(let i=0;i<3;i++){
    const res = await client.generate(req)
    if(res.status===429){
      const d = parseInt(res.headers['retry-after']||res.headers['x-rw-retry']||'1')
      await sleep(d*1000*Math.pow(2,i))
      continue
    }
    return res
  }
  throw new Error('rate limited')
}
```
Rae (Docs): Add one short trimming hint line: "drop oldest turns until estimated tokens fit; set partial=true when resuming."
Zoe (SDK): Streaming resume pseudo (omit imports):
```ts
// resume using resume_token and forward kv_cache_hint
async function resumeStream(resumeToken){
  return await client.generate({resume_token: resumeToken, kv_cache_hint: true})
}
```
Ivy (Eng Docs): Also a single-sentence guideline: "Use model-variant fallback for batch/background jobs where some quality drop is OK; prefer trimming to keep recent context in interactive sessions."
